   "text": "University of New Haven (Undergraduate) - QS Apply\nSkip to main content\nHOMEPAGE\nAPPLICATIONS\nNOTIFICATIONS\nEK\nUniversity of New Haven (Undergraduate)\nSummary\nDegrees and Programs\nStudent Testimonials\nCommission\nViewer Access\nAny user can see this institution.\nDescription\nThe University of New Haven (UNH) is a private university in West Haven, Connecticut. Between its main campus in West Haven and its graduate school campus in Orange, Connecticut, the university grounds cover about 122 acres of land. The university includes the College of Arts and Sciences, the Pompea College of Business, the Tagliatela College of Engineering, the Henry C. Lee College of Criminal Justice and Forensic Sciences, and the School of Health Sciences. The university is a member of the Northeast-10 Conference and its mascot is a charger, a medieval war horse.\nTimestamps\nUpdated\n26/03/2026 12:03\nby Eston Dalmeida\nCreated\n26/03/2026 12:03\nby Eston Dalmeida\nType\nUniversity\nCountry\nUnited States\nYearly Fees\nMax: US$43,000.00\nMin: US$16,200.00\nInternational Students\nPercentage of International Students\n10%\n700 of 7,000 Total Students\nOverview\nBasic Details\nInstitution Details\nOwnership\nPrivate\nProvider\nDirect QS\nFounded Year\n1920\nCampus(es)\nNew Haven, Connecticut\nCountry\nUnited States\nExcluded Countries\nNA\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\n No\nContract Start Date\n11/07/2022\nContract End Date\n01/01/2036\nContract Entity\nQSSA Ltd\nContract Status\nActive\nContract Document Link(s)\nN/A\nImages\nImages\nAdditional Details\nAccommodation Details\n-\nScholarship Offered\nMerit Based: $10,000 - $28,000 per year (Automatic consideration when applying). Transfer students: $12,000 - $24,000 per year (min 3.0 GPA). Honors: Additional $1,000 addition to Merit based\nYouTube Video Link(s)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hc8CX2y0mzE\nInternship Details\n-\nAdditional Information\n-",
